invariant: INV-14
file: handshake_parser_ee.c
catches: handshake_strict_webpki
reason: the server_certificate_type arm accepts either type this
  client knows instead of the types its ClientHello offered, so a
  pins-only client that offered RawPublicKey alone accepts X.509 and
  then reads a chain it has no anchor for. RFC 7250 §4.2 has a server
  with no type in common send unsupported_certificate rather than
  select outside the offer. bin/handshake_strict_webpki's
  offered-raw-alone row objects.

--- old
    if (!cert_type_offered(out->cert_types_offered, type)) {
--- new
    if (!cert_type_offered((1U << CH_CERT_TYPE_X509) | (1U << CH_CERT_TYPE_RAW_PUBLIC_KEY), type)) {
